        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
                "word": "surpopulation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f587d80d-5e6a-4c2d-ac2e-178125b6f16a",
                        "entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "surpopulations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5a52603-c76d-3201-9568-d80f6e13862e",
                        "entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Excès de population."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1f7ac6a-bb07-4ede-a462-c2b6475350a9",
                                "sense_id": "d5a52603-c76d-3201-9568-d80f6e13862e",
                                "text": "Alors que la surpopulation carcérale atteint des niveaux record en France, Rémy Heitz, le procureur général de Paris, a estimé, jeudi, qu’il « n’y [avait] pas de fatalité »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4ff8081-396f-4af5-aa16-378768f580d3",
                                "sense_id": "d5a52603-c76d-3201-9568-d80f6e13862e",
                                "text": "S'ils se sont répandus, nombreux, à travers d'autres pays, c'est soit pour fuir des catastrophes (guerres, révolutions, massacres,) soit pour échapper aux inconvénients de la surpopulation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "38bdc937-ccd6-42fd-81fa-3e46a1d90039",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
                        "source_sense_id": "d5a52603-c76d-3201-9568-d80f6e13862e",
                        "target_lang_word": "Überbevölkerung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Überbevölkerung",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf4b60fb-6326-3506-9fbd-bd8d6252d836",
                                        "entry_id": "988d9e67-6886-323d-a1f3-382a29ada393",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "zu große Zahl von Personen in einem Gebiet, die aus diesem Grund nicht hinreichend versorgt werden können"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "457ed855-9b87-47d1-81b9-c335c5a8845a",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4b60fb-6326-3506-9fbd-bd8d6252d836",
                                                "text": "„Im Jahr 1783 hatte die Überbevölkerung in den Städten bedrohliche Ausmaße angenommen - die entlassenen Soldaten einer gewaltigen Armee waren aus den Kriegen nach Hause zurückgekehrt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aad062a-01c6-4a71-a25d-7bcd5f1b3adb",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4b60fb-6326-3506-9fbd-bd8d6252d836",
                                                "text": "„Es könnte an einer Überbevölkerung, dem dadurch bedingten Nahrungsmangel und folgenden sozialen Unruhen gelegen haben.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c7ccf4b-51e3-4e1f-acfd-9e4c2d2c4a18",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
                        "source_sense_id": "d5a52603-c76d-3201-9568-d80f6e13862e",
                        "target_lang_word": "overpopulation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overpopulation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a51c704e-a435-38a4-9c78-151dbcf6dbbb",
                                        "entry_id": "e9bd54f2-5d4f-36a0-a04e-f87be667d8b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An excessive number of occupants (people, animals, plants, etc.) in a particular area; specifically, when the number of occupants exceeds the ability of that area to provide for them."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f364271f-0f7a-4dc0-b07e-6c4b18787b08",
                                                "sense_id": "a51c704e-a435-38a4-9c78-151dbcf6dbbb",
                                                "text": "I hope for another end, though not, indeed, from any of the three remedies for over-population commonly suggested by economists. These three are, in brief—Colonization; Bringing in of waste lands; or Discouragement of Marriage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a5ceac2-1fd6-4adb-8e8e-9ea1c949f5e7",
                                                "sense_id": "a51c704e-a435-38a4-9c78-151dbcf6dbbb",
                                                "text": "Over the whole extent of the South Seas, from one tropic to another, we find traces of a bygone state of over-population, when the resources of even a tropical soil were taxed, and even the improvident Polynesian trembled for the future."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98fd3fda-da60-4d2f-94c4-3df57e6b034d",
                                                "sense_id": "a51c704e-a435-38a4-9c78-151dbcf6dbbb",
                                                "text": "When it comes to overpopulation as the cause of wildlife loss in Africa, Prince William just won't let it go."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac74609f-77bf-43a8-9621-01941822a02f",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed985418-182e-3420-86e7-796e57062b13",
